{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And he made the holy anointing oil and the pure incense of spices</b> — He did not elaborate on these as he elaborated on the others, for by way of the rest it would have been fitting to say: 'And he took principal spices, pure myrrh, etc.' (Exodus 30:23), 'and he made it a holy anointing oil'; 'And he took spices, stacte, onycha, etc.' (Exodus 30:34), 'and he made it incense, a compound after the art of the perfumer.' The reason is that because the command was not stated for them with the completion of the making, as I explained there (above, 30:25, 34), and in the case of the incense he also did not mention all the spices, but relied on them by what he said 'after the art of the perfumer' — in the account of the making he mentioned none of them at all, but said only that they made it according to the understanding of the perfumers. And this is the meaning of <b>'holy, pure, after the art of the perfumer.'</b>"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:22:02.453238181Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}